From f2fe655aecf576341cb439357070d0bb3ad25b5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omalawn <omalawn@local>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 13:17:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] omalawn link: TLS server, foreground service, mDNS

Mutual TLS 1.3 server on TCP 47100 with an EC P-256 identity held in Android
Keystore, JSON-line and blob framing, per-request pin classification, a
connectedDevice foreground service with a status notification, boot/update
receiver and an _omalawn._tcp mDNS advert. Dispatcher gains link.hello,
link.ping and launcher.apps_list; layout, prefs and wallpaper calls run one at
a time; wallpaper backup cleanup only removes stale files. Debug-build pin hooks
on the shell-only provider.

Pairing by four words (SAS over both certificates and both nonces, BIP-39
list as an asset): link.pair_request (nonce commitment) / link.pair_reveal /
link.pair_wait / link.unpair, a single
pairing slot that outlives the unpaired lifetime, a Homa Lawn Accept/Reject
notification that needs an unlocked phone, rate limit 3 per 10 minutes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ArQxcgsGx5uG8agkURxU2Z
